==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
{{etyl|xno|en}} and {{etyl|fro|en}} {{term|arson|lang=fro}}, from the verb {{term|ardoir|lang=fro}}, from {{etyl|la|en}} {{m|la|ardeō||to burn}}. Compare {{term|ardent|lang=en}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈɑː(ɹ)sən/|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~|arsons}}

# {{context|uncountable|lang=en}} The [[crime]] of [[set]]ting a [[fire]] with [[intent]] to [[cause]] [[damage]].
#* '''2006''', [[w:Paul Chadwick|Paul Chadwick]], ''Concrete: Killer Smile'', Part two, p.34
#*: '''Arson''', like we thought.  three punks doused a car, lit it, and took off.
# {{context|countable|lang=en}} An instance of such a crime.

